<spell-notebook "actions usage">
	<header level="1">
		Actions
		<header>Actions hold what a user can do next:  a comment's reply links, a modal's or toast's buttons.</>
	</>
	<actions-tab-bar showing="usage"/>
	<section>
		<menu class="ui-docs-section-tabs" appearance="segmented" aria-label="Sections">
			<item link="#using-it">Using it</>
			<item link="#owners">Owners</>
			<item link="#accessibility">Accessibility</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Using it">
		<markdown>
			`<ui-actions>` holds what a user can do next with its owner's content: a comment's reply links, a modal's or
			flyout's buttons. Put links or `<ui-button>`s inside it; it lays them out the way its owner expects (a comment's
			links in a row, a modal's buttons on the right, on a footer band).

			- No attributes: the owner decides the look.
			- A button's `class="approve"` / `class="deny"` in a modal's actions closes the modal (see the modal page).
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Owners">
		<markdown>
			`<ui-actions>` finds its nearest owner and sets `:state(in-<owner>)` on itself; `UIParts.css` styles it by that
			state. Its owners, and what each makes of it:

			- [Comment](/components/ui/ui-comment.html) (`:state(in-comment)`): a row of small, quiet links under the text; `minimal` comments show them on hover or focus
			- [Modal](/components/ui/ui-modal.html) (`:state(in-modal)`): the footer band, buttons on the right
			- [Flyout](/components/ui/ui-flyout.html) (`:state(in-flyout)`): the footer band, buttons on the right
			- [Toast](/components/ui/ui-toast.html) (`:state(in-toast)`): buttons under the message

			Anywhere else it is an unstyled block. More on how parts find their owners: [Content parts](/components/ui/ui-header.html).
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Accessibility">
		<markdown>
			- A neutral block with no role: the links and buttons inside it carry the meaning, so give icon-only buttons an
			  `aria-label`.
			- A comment's `minimal` actions show on hover AND on keyboard focus, so they stay reachable with **Tab**.
		</>
	</>
</spell-notebook>
